  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Determination\\n\\nExpect **`InvalidCursorError`** from `@ordarium/core` — `OrdariumError` subclass with `code === \\\"INVALID_CURSOR\\\"` and message *\\\"The change cursor is not a valid durable position; refusing to guess a resume point\\\"*. A rejected stored observation (change‑feed) cursor is a **dedicated, fail‑closed input error**, not a generic ledger failure.\\n\\n## Why — provenance reasoning\\n\\n**1. Which Ordarium line actually governs this workspace.** The load‑bearing pin is `@ordarium/*` **1.3.1**, stated in three mutually reinforcing places:\\n- `package.json:32–37` (all four packages, `ordarium-v1.3.1` release tarballs);\\n- `pnpm-workspace.yaml:15–18` `overrides` — which `07-ordarium-alignment.md` §3.1 r2 勘误 declares the *authoritative* location for these pins;\\n- the installed artifacts themselves: `node_modules/@ordarium/core` and `node_modules/@ordarium/ledger-sqlite`, whose code is version 1.3.1.\\n\\n`docs/engineering/07-ordarium-alignment.md` still registers 1.2.0 and never mentions a 1.3.x bump, but it is a stale record (its revision log stops at PLMP-CONF‑1/1.2.0), not the pin. It does not assert any cursor‑rejection behavior, so it is not a competing behavioral source",
